WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.780
We all love shopping and eating out!

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.680
But ever been in a situation where you spent more than you intended to?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.800
Probably every time!

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.180
What makes you to spend more?

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.340
Is it the offer? Or the price? Or is it something else?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.060
Do you think your decisions are really controlled by you?

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.880
Let’s find out.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.760
The answer to this could be the Decoy effect.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.840
What does it mean?

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.640
It simply means change in preference between two options

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.560
when presented with a third one.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.200
Confusing right?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.540
Let’s make this simpler for you.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.520
You’re in a movie theater

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.380
and you've been given two options for some delicious popcorn!

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.460
A small popcorn bucket costs 4 dollars,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.000
and a large popcorn bucket costs 8 dollars.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:59.000
Most of us want more; but as we intend to spend less,

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.860
we would choose the cheaper option.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.800
But the company obviously wants you to buy the large popcorn bucket!

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.960
What would they do?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.720
One option could be to give a discount for the large bucket!

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.000
But there’s an even better alternative!

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.220
They add a third option called the decoy.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.360
They now give you an option of medium sized popcorn bucket

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.300
for 7 dollars and fifty cents!

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.420
Which one would you buy now?

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.460
Most of us would opt for the large sized bucket

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.520
as this now seems better value for money.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.780
The decoy option that is the medium sized bucket

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.560
makes the human mind make inaccurate judgments!

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.160
Notice that the decoy is priced really close to the more expensive option,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.640
making the more expensive option look significantly better.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.680
It’s so skewed on purpose,

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:57.020
that it seems stupid, to not choose the higher-priced option!

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.060
Alright! Now, instead of pricing the medium sized bucket

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.480
for 7 dollars and fifty cents,

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.260
what if it is priced for 4 dollars and fifty cents?

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.820
Which one would you choose now?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.420
Obviously the medium sized popcorn bucket!

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.320
Because this looks better than the small sized popcorn bucket.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.500
Don’t you think the small sized bucket is acting as the decoy here?

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.100
Yes!

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.740
So now tell me, is the decision to choose anything here controlled by you?

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.640
Definitely not!

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.240
The visual illusion is deliberately created by the company

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.380
to alter your judgments.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.580
Thus, you take an irrational decision from the given options.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.040
Is the decoy effect only price related?

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.920
Absolutely not!

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.180
Let’s say you’re planning to dine out with your friends.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.420
Your preferences are quality and ambiance over price.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.020
Here are the choices available in your vicinity.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.340
It is very clear from the options that your obvious choice

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.720
would be the five star restaurant.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.280
It is just a matter of half a kilometer more than the

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.180
four star restaurant to experience your desired ambience.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.940
So, the best option is this one!

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.720
Here, the four star restaurant acted as the decoy.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.680
Alright, let’s say we remove the decoy here.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.680
What would your choice of preference be now?

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.440
Well, the same five star restaurant now looks like a long distance to cover.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.580
So in this case, we would generally settle with option one.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:39.140
We saw how the decoy effect plays with our judgments in our day-to-day lives!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.720
Can we use the decoy effect for any social cause?

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.620
Let’s say your city is planning a campaign to plant trees.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.960
You want maximum people to participate in the campaign

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.880
and also plant more number of trees.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.040
Can you come up with a plan using the decoy effect

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.020
to motivate people to plant trees?

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.800
This is one of the ways which we could think of!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.240
Will this work?

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:10.380
Notice, that here we haven’t used money as a reward.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:15.740
Can you come up with more such plans without using money as the reward?

